---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CinematicBackground from '../../components/CinematicBackground.astro';
import ExpandableContent from '../../components/ExpandableContent.astro';
---

<Layout title="The Library | EdLove">
    <CinematicBackground />

    <section class="relative z-10 min-h-screen flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center px-6 pt-24 pb-12">
        <h1 class="font-cinzel text-warmGold text-xl md:text-2xl tracking-[0.2em] uppercase mb-4">Domain VI</h1>
        <h2 class="font-serif text-5xl md:text-7xl text-[#2D3561] mb-6">The Epistemic Core</h2>
        
        <p class="font-sans text-lg md:text-xl text-[#2D3561]/80 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed mb-12">
            This is the space for wondering. We explore the <strong>what, why, and how</strong> of education—and the temporal dimensions of these questions. 
            From philosophy to neuroscience, from ancient history to the future of cognition.
        </p>

        <div class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-12 transform hover:scale-[1.01] transition-all duration-500 cursor-pointer shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(212,165,116,0.1)]">
            <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-warmGold/20 via-dawnRose/20 to-cosmicPurple/20 border border-[#D4A574]/30 rounded-xl p-8 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-8 text-left backdrop-blur-md">
                <div class="text-6xl animate-pulse">⚡</div>
                <div>
                    <span class="font-sans text-xs text-[#D4A574] uppercase tracking-widest font-bold">Featured Innovation</span>
                    <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl md:text-4xl text-[#2D3561] mb-2">Teaning</h3>
                    <p class="font-sans text-[#2D3561]/80 leading-relaxed">
                        The Relational Framework for Understanding Educational Transformation. <br/>
                        Matching impedance between teacher and student.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-4 text-left">
            <ExpandableContent title="Thinkers" subtitle="The Giants" icon="🧠" mode="panel">
                <p class="text-xl font-serif text-[#D4A574] mb-4">"We climb on the shoulders of giants to see further."</p>
                <p>Education has been debated for millennia. Here we profile the visionaries who dared to rethink the transmission of culture.</p>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6">
                    <div>
                        <strong class="text-[#2D3561]">Maria Montessori</strong>
                        <p class="text-sm text-[#2D3561]/70">The scientist of childhood. Discovered that freedom within limits leads to discipline.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <strong class="text-[#2D3561]">Paulo Freire</strong>
                        <p class="text-sm text-[#2D3561]/70">The liberator. Taught us that education is either domestication or the practice of freedom.</p>
                    </div>
                     <div>
                        <strong class="text-[#2D3561]">J. Krishnamurti</strong>
                        <p class="text-sm text-[#2D3561]/70">The seer. Asked us to look at the conditioning of our own minds before we teach others.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </ExpandableContent>
            
            <ExpandableContent title="Frameworks" subtitle="Mental Models" icon="📐" mode="panel">
                <p class="text-xl font-serif text-[#D4A574] mb-4">"Maps of Meaning."</p>
                <p>We use rigorous intellectual tools to understand the complexity of schools, brains, and societies. This is not just opinion; it is structural analysis.</p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-4 text-[#2D3561]/70 space-y-2">
                    <li><strong>Integral Theory (Ken Wilber):</strong> Mapping the subjective, objective, cultural, and systemic dimensions of learning.</li>
                    <li><strong>Spiral Dynamics:</strong> Understanding the evolution of value systems in students and institutions.</li>
                    <li><strong>Systems Thinking:</strong> Seeing the feedback loops, delays, and leverage points in the education sector.</li>
                </ul>
            </ExpandableContent>

            <ExpandableContent title="Stories" subtitle="Narratives of Change" icon="📖" mode="panel">
                <p>History is written by the victors, but the future is written by the experimenters. Case studies of schools that broke the mold.</p>
            </ExpandableContent>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>
